The action log lands here (see compose.yml's ./audit:/audit mount).

This directory is COMMITTED, empty, on purpose. Docker creates a missing bind
source as root, and bothy-ops runs as uid 1000, so an absent directory would
be mounted and unwritable - and audit() swallows that error by design, because a
full disk must never block a legitimate restart. The symptom would therefore be
a silently empty log rather than a failure, which is the worst way for an audit
trail to be broken. Committing the directory means it is always there and always
owned by whoever cloned the repo.

Both halves of bothy-ops write here since 2026-09 (container actions and cluster
actions, one actions.log). apps/bothy-files declares the same kind of mount and
does NOT commit its directory; bootstrap creates it.
